From: clawd20130 <clawd20130@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 16:49:54 +0900
Subject: Android host backend: display settings and idle inhibition in
 src/backends/android

kwin_wayland --android-host selects AndroidBackend, a WaylandBackend for KWin nested in
the Android host compositor (the APK). What only that host needs lives in
src/backends/android; upstream files carry small hooks:

- main_wayland.cpp: the --android-host option.
- WaylandBackend::createOutputObject(): protected virtual, so the backend makes its own outputs.
- WaylandOutput::modesFor(), applyExtraChanges(): protected virtual, plus setRefreshRate().
- InputRedirection::idleInhibitedChanged(bool): emitted when the first window starts or the
  last one stops inhibiting idle.

AndroidOutput offers the Android display's resolutions x refresh rates on the phone output,
which is internal and gets the physical size Android reports; on every output of the host
KWin owns the scale (the host shows KWin's buffer 1:1). AndroidBackend asks Android to switch
resolution or refresh policy when the user changes the phone output (not a cast output), and
forwards idle inhibition as a standard zwp_idle_inhibitor_v1 on the phone output's surface,
bound on a queue of its own; the host keeps the screen on while it exists (APK 1.46). This
replaces the D-Bus call to dev.moto.Android.Power and its 5 s re-sends, and the display code
that was spread over wayland_backend.cpp and wayland_output.cpp behind MOTO_KWIN_FLAT_OUTPUT.

Forwarded: not-needed
